BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:OLZyqzuCKeNcOwqLe1704
SUMMARY:Influencer–Brand Partnerships: A Matching Approach
DTSTAMP:20260731T111648Z
DTSTART:20260803T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;  Speaker: Masoud Jabbari  Doctoral Candidate  Thesis De
	fense  Department: Economics  Location: Kraft Hall 102  This thesis studie
	s how brands allocate advertising budgets across bundles of Instagram infl
	uencers in a centralized platform\, addressing the business problem of pla
	tform assignment potentially overriding brand preferences. I develop a str
	uctural matching model to recover preferences over influencer scale\, enga
	gement\, and thematic focus\, estimated conditional on campaign characteri
	stics using administrative platform data. Preferences are identified using
	 pairwise stability\, first in matches alone and then jointly in matches a
	nd prices\, leveraging influencer posted prices and a control-function app
	roach based on hedonic regressions to address price endogeneity and persis
	tent unobserved quality. The estimates indicate that follower count is mos
	t valuable for follower-growth campaigns\, whereas engagement and thematic
	 concentration become relatively more important for sales- and lead-genera
	tion objectives. Counterfactual analyses highlight the important role of N
	ano and Micro influencers in maintaining brand utility and demonstrate tha
	t platform assignments in CPM campaigns can be substantially improved when
	 aligned with estimated preferences. Methodologically\, this thesis demons
	trates how preferences can be recovered in platform-mediated matching envi
	ronments with limited choice-set observability\, providing a tractable fra
	mework for analyzing digital advertising markets and informing more effect
	ive platform allocation design.  &#160\;  (Department : Economics)\n\nhttp
	s://events.rice.edu/live/events/435072-influencerbrand-partnerships-a-matc
	hing-approach\n\nFrom Rice University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/live/events/435072-influencerbrand-partnerships
	-a-matching-approach
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:Kraft Hall
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston
 .com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/52nd-Annual-Houston-Shakespeare-Festival-T
 he-Tempest-at-Miller-Outdoor-Theatre.jpeg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston.com/wp-content/uploads
 /2026/07/52nd-Annual-Houston-Shakespeare-Festival-The-Tempest-at-Miller-Ou
 tdoor-Theatre.jpeg
UID:xPYQBzxB8Yy7WROUMne3N
SUMMARY:52nd Annual Houston Shakespeare Festival: The Tempest at Miller Out
	door Theatre
DTSTAMP:20260731T111648Z
DTSTART:20260803T201500Z
DESCRIPTION:Houston Shakespeare Festival\, the city’s annual summer theater
	 tradition\, celebrates its 52nd season with performances of both The Temp
	est and Comedy of Errors on alternating nights at Miller Outdoor Theatre. 
	\nShakespeare’s The Tempest\nExiled by her brother to a remote island and 
	left to die\, Prospera—the once loved Duchess of Milan and now an all-powe
	rful sorceress—conjures a great tempest to wash ashore a ship of her enemi
	es. \nWith the power of magic\, Prospera manipulates the survivors of the 
	wreckage to weave a story of revenge\, retribution\, and reconciliation. R
	ich with spectacle\, humor and wonder\, Shakespeare’s final play brings au
	diences to a “brave new world ” where reconciliation is possible and human
	ity is renewed. \nFinding Your Seat at Miller Outdoor Theatre\nAs always\,
	 all seats at Miller are free\, but covered seating for popular evening sh
	ows usually requires a free assigned ticket reserved 24 hours in advance. 
	\nLearn more about getting free seated tickets at Miller. \nAdmission\nFre
	e. Learn more or reserve a free seated ticket. \n \nThis Featured Calendar
	 Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our calendar 
	with images and more details.  \nLearn more about promoting your event\, o
	rganization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.\n\nhttps://3
	65thingsinhouston.com/calendar/52nd-annual-houston-shakespeare-festival-th
	e-tempest-at-miller-outdoor-theatre-3/\n\nFrom 365 Things to Do in Houston
